From: GameShellNeo maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: stop deferred registration before notification work

Deferred registration calls power_supply_changed(). Cancelling changed_work
first leaves a window for an already running deferred callback to queue it
again while unregister joins deferred_register_work. Unregister need not hold
the parent device lock, for example when a runtime worker removes a supply.

Join that producer first, then cancel its notification work before releasing
the supply. Keep the existing parent-trylock/removing escape so callers holding
the parent lock can still join deferred registration without deadlocking.
Other notification producers must still be retired by their owners.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/power_supply_core.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/power_supply_core.c
@@ -1760,8 +1760,9 @@
 {
 	WARN_ON(atomic_dec_return(&psy->use_cnt));
 	psy->removing = true;
+	/* Stop the producer before draining the notifications it can queue. */
+	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&psy->deferred_register_work);
 	cancel_work_sync(&psy->changed_work);
-	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&psy->deferred_register_work);
 	sysfs_remove_link(&psy->dev.kobj, "powers");
 	power_supply_remove_hwmon_sysfs(psy);
 	power_supply_remove_triggers(psy);
